WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.933
In block zero, eight threads copy the

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:05.018
values one through eight into shared

00:00:05.018 --> 00:00:07.451
memory. Each slot belongs to one thread

00:00:07.451 --> 00:00:08.841
during this first load.

00:00:13.341 --> 00:00:15.630
All threads reach the barrier. Thread one

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.247
then reads the six stored by thread five.

00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:24.994
At distance four, thread one adds the

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:27.884
value in slot five to its own slot. What

00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:29.168
will slot one contain?

00:00:37.669 --> 00:00:40.531
Thread one adds two and six and stores

00:00:40.531 --> 00:00:42.677
eight. The other active threads update

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:45.181
their slots too. A barrier completes the

00:00:45.181 --> 00:00:46.970
stage before the next distance.
